How this directory was made
---------------------------
The 17 files under packages/instrumenter/test/unit/mutators/*-mutator.spec.ts at v10.0.0,
fetched through the GitHub contents API and copied here byte for byte. Not one edit, not
even to the import specifiers: compat/vitest.config.ts resolves the specs' imports of
`../../../src/mutators/*.js` and `../../helpers/expect-mutation.js` to oxmutate's shims, so
Stryker's own tables grade oxmutate's native core (SC9, .sdlc/intents/oxmutate/intent.md).

What is graded, and what is not
-------------------------------
Each `expectJSMutation(mutator, input, context, ...expected)` runs `input` through
oxmutate's instrumenter, keeps the mutants of that mutator's family, and requires exactly
`expected` — compared after both sides are printed by one printer, because Stryker prints a
replaced node through @babel/generator and oxmutate edits the source span, and the two
format a statement differently while meaning the same program.

Tests of Stryker's internals rather than its mutants are listed, each with its reason, in
compat/not-applicable.ts; they are skipped by name, never edited.

Reproduce
---------
    for f in $(gh api "repos/stryker-mutator/stryker-js/git/trees/v10.0.0?recursive=1" --jq '.tree[].path' \
        | grep -E 'packages/instrumenter/test/unit/mutators/.*-mutator\.spec\.ts$'); do
      gh api "repos/stryker-mutator/stryker-js/contents/$f?ref=v10.0.0" --jq .content | base64 -d \
        > packages/oxmutate/vendor/stryker-mutators/test/unit/mutators/$(basename "$f")
    done
